n","ext":".json","contentType":"application/json","contentLength":63307,"name":"newspec-c/evidence/hallu/hallu-nh/grading/TC-14-S46-HL-N5-B.judge.json"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"96a6f93547744de0f30ede7225811fcf","originalFileName":"ecc839aa-b522-4685-96cc-04d5438c2650-attachment.json","ext":".json","contentType":"application/json","contentLength":6273,"name":"lane result (newspec-c/results.json)"},"type":"attachment"}],"error":{"message":"newspec-c: record-only → needs a person (record only, the lane says it cannot decide / a person decides → a person looks)\nDev <dev address> (main 8b4be94a), live models (every call Haiku 4.5 us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0, no fallback; generateNote providerMs 7.1–15.1 s, parsePreRoundNotes 4.5–5.3 s), under runs/.dev.lock, browsers in UTC; datasets hallu-hosp + hallu-nh (new specs hallu-hosp/-nh.spec.ts + hallu-lib.ts), 10 synthetic fixtures (5 Hospital, 5 Nursing Home) × arm A (pre-round Save Note → summary → Encounter → Generate) and arm B (same words in the Encounter only → Generate); only prefixed rows created, all deleted (0 remaining, 0 changes to other rows). Trap verdicts by the fixture regexes, 13 'unclear'/false hits settled by the agent's reading (review.agent.json, a person confirms). Preston-kit judge (grade.mjs, claude-opus-5-5 ×2) on all 20 notes: 20/20 uncalibrated FAIL (U1 on every note, U2 on 16), beside, needs a person. 11 trap inventions in all. First stage: both summary and A note 5 (HL-H2 ICU, HL-H5 asthma, HL-H5 obesity, HL-N1 hypothyroidism, HL-N4 BPH), note only 3 (HL-H2 CAP, HL-H3 nephrology, HL-N3 hypertension), summary only 2 (HL-H3 hyperkalemia, HL-N1 'Viral URI'), B note only 1 (HL-N5 dialysis counselling). Of the 5 that were in the summary, 4 (all medication/number → diagnosis) are absent from the B note: the summary's background bullets are where they start (hypothesis holds for that family). The 3 note-only ones (and the ICU line) also appear without any summary: the note model invents them from the raw words (hypothesis does not cover them).…"},"testCase":{"id":"fce49b0607808d53b882fb3f96f736b9","externalId":"69a605214691892ec1728e9b6eba279d","name":"[dev] S45 Where the invention starts: pre-round summary vs. the note (arm A real flow vs. arm B no summary, same words)","fullName":"TC-14 In-Room Dictation & Note Generation › TC-14/S45"},"descriptionHtml":"<p><b>Case priority: P0 · stated in the UAT / ticket AC</b> · UAT 3.4; TFA-92592 AC 5; TFA-95204 AC 2 · “No diagnosis, medication decision, or action appears in the note unless it was dictated or typed”.</p><div class=\"rc-approach\"><p><b>Approach</b> · TC-14 In-Room Dictation &amp; Note Generation · <b>S45</b> Where the invention starts: pre-round summary vs. the note (arm A real flow vs. arm B no summary, same words)</p><p><b>UAT steps / ticket ACs covered:</b></p><ul><li><b>U5</b> The note reflects only what was dictated or stored, and undictated sections read 'Not dictated'. No supplied diagnosis, invented exam finding or normal, guessed unit on an ambiguous value, 'No past m … (UAT TC-14; UAT 3.4; TFA-92592 AC 5; TFA-94229 R8) — gate: blocked: TFA-92592 ready for pr; TFA-94229 in progress</li><li><b>U18</b> No diagnosis, medication decision or action appears in the note unless it was dictated or typed (&quot;the app documents, the physician decides&quot;): a drug never implies its indication, a value never become … (TFA-95204 AC 2; TFA-95204 AC 3; UAT 3.4; TFA-92592 AC 5)</li><li><b>T4</b> No dictated fact silently disappears from the note (Principle 2). (TFA-94229 R9) — gate: blocked: TFA-94229 in progress</li><li><b>U14</b> Steps 1 to 4 are repeated in Nursing Home, and every expected result holds in both Hospital and Nursing Home. (UAT TC-14 step 5; UAT 3.3; TFA-92592 AC 14) — gate: blocked: TFA-92592 ready for pr</li></ul><p><b>Test design technique: </b>Decision table (decision-table) — List the combinations of several conditions and check each one, to see that the result follows the rule.</p><p><b>Given </b>The ten fixtures of S40–S44, each run twice: A with the pre-round summary, B without it</p><p><b>When </b>Per trap: stage A-summary (stored after Save Note), stage A-note, stage B-note</p><p><b>Then </b>Decision table per invention: in summary and in A note → the summary carried it (hypothesis holds for that trap); A note only → the note model invented it from the raw text; B note too → it does not need the summary; summary only → the note did not take it over</p><p><b>Pass rule (oracle, excerpt): </b>Record only (diagnostic for TFA-95204 AC 1, 'find the difference'): the table of first stages; no pass / fail of its own</p><p><b>Where it ran: </b>newspec-c (new Playwright specs) on dev; test method AICHECK · AI output check; lane planned in the matrix: AI check (automated)</p><p><small>S45 is our own case number (its number in the coverage matrix cases/TC-14.matrix.json), not a step number of the UAT document.</small></p></div><p><b>Environment: dev</b> — dev deployment, build <code>8b4be94</code> (Deploy Convex, 2026-10-19T17:04:37Z); account and address are not written into the report; run folder <code>runs/2026-10-14-dev</code>, lane newspec-c (<code>newspec-c/results.json</code>, screenshots not attached).</p><p><b>Test method:</b> AICHECK · AI output check — as the lane wrote it; Source: <code>dev/newspec-c</code>.</p><p><b>UAT item:</b> TC-14 In-Room Dictation &amp; Note Generation · <b>Section:</b> A3 · Encounter · <b>Scenario:</b> TC-14/S45</p><p><b>Where the invention starts: pre-round summary vs. the note (arm A real flow vs. arm B no summary, same words)</b></p><p><b>Tickets:</b> TFA-92592 In-Room Dictation &amp; Note Generation (ready for qa)</p><p><b>Lane in the dev run folder</b> <code>newspec-c</code>: status <b>record-only</b> in <code>newspec-c/results.json</code> → <b>needs a person</b> (record only, the lane says it cannot decide / a person decides → a person looks).</p><p><b>Detail:</b></p><pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">Dev <dev address> (main 8b4be94a), live models (every call Haiku 4.5 us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0, no fallback; generateNote providerMs 7.1–15.1 s, parsePreRoundNotes 4.5–5.3 s), under runs/.dev.lock, browsers in UTC; datasets hallu-hosp + hallu-nh (new specs hallu-hosp/-nh.spec.ts + hallu-lib.ts), 10 synthetic fixtures (5 Hospital, 5 Nursing Home) × arm A (pre-round Save Note → summary → Encounter → Generate) and arm B (same words in the Encounter only → Generate); only prefixed rows created, all deleted (0 remaining, 0 changes to other rows). Trap verdicts by the fixture regexes, 13 'unclear'/false hits settled by the agent's reading (review.agent.json, a person confirms). Preston-kit judge (grade.mjs, claude-opus-5-5 ×2) on all 20 notes: 20/20 uncalibrated FAIL (U1 on every note, U2 on 16), beside, needs a person. 11 trap inventions in all. First stage: both summary and A note 5 (HL-H2 ICU, HL-H5 asthma, HL-H5 obesity, HL-N1 hypothyroidism, HL-N4 BPH), note only 3 (HL-H2 CAP, HL-H3 nephrology, HL-N3 hypertension), summary only 2 (HL-H3 hyperkalemia, HL-N1 'Viral URI'), B note only 1 (HL-N5 dialysis counselling). Of the 5 that were in the summary, 4 (all medication/number → diagnosis) are absent from the B note: the summary's background bullets are where they start (hypothesis holds for that family). The 3 note-only ones (and the ICU line) also appear without any summary: the note model invents them from the raw words (hypothesis does not cover them). Hospital notes get the summary as backgroundSummary (lib/noteInput.ts), Nursing Home notes as background.</pre><p><b>Evidence:</b> 42 attached.</p><p><b>Dev run:</b> not run — Not in the run plan.. This dev newspec-c result replaces that dev entry (the scenario appears once).</p>","environment":"default","setup":[],"teardown":[],"history":[],"retries":[],"breadcrumbs":[["TC-14 In-Room Dictation & Note Generation","S45 Where the invention starts: pre-round summa